{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-70824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the Cartesian equation $7y-z-13=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-70824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨0,7,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7y-z-13 & =0 \\\\ z & =7y-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $y=0$, we get $z=-13.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-13)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-13⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,-1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-70824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a0ff5befc88cb0e6d2fc3acf82014f4117fbe4bb16105e0afabc5c7206f3472a"} {"question" "q-70824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-70824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,-1⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,7,-1⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,-1,-13⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,-1⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,13⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,-1,-13⟩=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-70824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,-1⟩=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-128383" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the Cartesian equation $5y-z+17=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-128383" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨0,5,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-z+17 & =0 \\\\ z & =5y+17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $y=0$, we get $z=17.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,17)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,17⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,17⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,5,-1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-128383" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a0ff5befc88cb0e6d2fc3acf82014f4117fbe4bb16105e0afabc5c7206f3472a"} {"question" "q-128383" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-128383" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(r-⟨0,0,-15⟩)\\cdot ⟨-1,5,0⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,-21⟩)\\cdot ⟨5,0,-1⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,11⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,5,1⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,-1,5⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,17⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,5,-1⟩=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-128383" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(r-⟨0,0,17⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,5,-1⟩=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-330500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,1,-5)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-330500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨2,1,-5⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =⟨2,1,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =10 \\\\ 6x-2y & =10 \\\\ 6x-2y-10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-330500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a0ff5befc88cb0e6d2fc3acf82014f4117fbe4bb16105e0afabc5c7206f3472a"} {"question" "q-330500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-330500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6x+y-10=0"] ["math" "6x-2y+z-10=0"] ["math" "6x-2y-10=0"] ["math" "6x-y-10z=0"] ["math" "x-6y-10=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-330500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6x-2y-10=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-4,3,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-3,-6⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,2,-8⟩.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$y\\,+\\,z\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-4,3,5⟩.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =36i+16j+4k \\\\  & =⟨36,16,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ & =⟨-4,3,5⟩\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ & =-76\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ & =-76 \\\\ 36x+16y+4z & =-76 \\\\ 36x+16y+4z+76 & =0 \\\\ 9x+4y+z+19 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a0ff5befc88cb0e6d2fc3acf82014f4117fbe4bb16105e0afabc5c7206f3472a"} {"question" "q-336358" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336358" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336358" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336358" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336358" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336358" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "19"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-3,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,-3,1⟩.$ From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨4,0,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is\n\n$$\nn=⟨4,0,-2⟩,\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ & =⟨2,-3,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute  $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ & =3 \\\\ 4x-2z & =6 \\\\ 4x-2z-6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a0ff5befc88cb0e6d2fc3acf82014f4117fbe4bb16105e0afabc5c7206f3472a"} {"question" "q-336407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x+y-2z-3=0"] ["math" "4x+y+2z-3=0"] ["math" "4x+y-2z-5=0"] ["math" "4x-2z-6=0"] ["math" "4x-y-2z-3=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"} {"question" "q-336407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x-2z-6=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053060/state.json" "file_sha256" "614e4b0de64e10145ee68650a15fc17d28554c286233c96666af4e571a4c5933"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1777 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
